<article class="env-definition" id="013W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/013W">Definition <span data-tag="013W">13.23.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category with enough injectives. A <em>resolution functor</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000268204" id="a0000268204-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> for $\mathcal{A}$ is given by the following data: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
for all $K^\bullet \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (K^{+}(\mathcal{A}))$ a bounded below complex of injectives $j(K^\bullet )$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for all $K^\bullet \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (K^{+}(\mathcal{A}))$ a quasi-isomorphism $i_{K^\bullet } : K^\bullet \to j(K^\bullet )$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>